@@ -0,0 +1,309 @@
+.\"-
+.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
+.\"
+.\" Copyright (c) 2026 Kyle Crenshaw <b1nc0d3x@gmail.com>
+.\"
+.Dd October 12, 2026
+.Dt IEEE80211_FULLMAC 9
+.Os
+.Sh NAME
+.Nm ieee80211_fullmac
+.Nd 802.11 network layer support for FullMAC devices
+.Sh SYNOPSIS
+.In net80211/ieee80211_var.h
+.In net80211/ieee80211_fullmac.h
+.Ft int
+.Fo ieee80211_fmac_attach
+.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Fa "const struct ieee80211_fullmac_ops *ops"
+.Fc
+.Ft void
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_detach "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Ft void
+.Fo ieee80211_fmac_scan_result
+.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Fa "const struct ieee80211_fmac_bss *bss"
+.Fc
+.Ft void
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_scan_done "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Ft int
+.Fo ieee80211_fmac_link_up
+.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Fa "const uint8_t bssid[IEEE80211_ADDR_LEN]"
+.Fc
+.Ft int
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_link_down "struct ieee80211com *ic" "uint16_t reason"
+.Ft int
+.Fo ieee80211_fmac_roamed
+.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Fa "const struct ieee80211_fmac_bss *bss"
+.Fc
+.Ft void
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_rx "struct ieee80211com *ic" "struct mbuf *m"
+.Ft void
+.Fo ieee80211_fmac_sta_join
+.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Fa "const uint8_t mac[IEEE80211_ADDR_LEN]"
+.Fa "const uint8_t *ies"
+.Fa "size_t ielen"
+.Fa "bool reassoc"
+.Fc
+.Ft void
+.Fo ieee80211_fmac_sta_leave
+.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Fa "const uint8_t mac[IEEE80211_ADDR_LEN]"
+.Fa "uint16_t reason"
+.Fc
+.Ft void
+.Fo ieee80211_fmac_extauth_req
+.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Fa "const uint8_t bssid[IEEE80211_ADDR_LEN]"
+.Fa "const uint8_t *ssid"
+.Fa "size_t ssid_len"
+.Fc
+.Ft void
+.Fo ieee80211_fmac_mgmt_rx
+.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Fa "const uint8_t *frame"
+.Fa "size_t len"
+.Fa "uint16_t freq"
+.Fa "int8_t rssi"
+.Fc
+.Ft void
+.Fo ieee80211_fmac_assoc_reject
+.Fa "struct ieee80211com *ic"
+.Fa "const uint8_t bssid[IEEE80211_ADDR_LEN]"
+.Fa "uint16_t status"
+.Fc
+.Sh DESCRIPTION
+A FullMAC device runs scanning, authentication, association and often
+the key handshake in its own firmware, and exchanges Ethernet frames
+with the host.
+The
+.Xr ieee80211 9
+layer is built for devices that exchange 802.11 frames and leave those
+steps to the host.
+The
+.Nm
+framework sits between the two.
+A driver describes what its firmware can do with a table of operations,
+and reports what the firmware tells it through a small set of calls.
+The framework keeps
+.Xr ieee80211 9 ,
+.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
+.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
+and
+.Xr hostapd 8
+working as they do with any other wireless device.
+.Pp
+The driver calls
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_attach
+after
+.Xr ieee80211_ifattach 9
+and after setting
+.Va ic_vap_create ,
+which the framework wraps to set up each vap the driver creates.
+The framework takes over the
+.Vt ieee80211com
+methods for scanning, regulatory changes and signal reports, and the
+state, key and
+.Xr ioctl 2
+methods of each vap the driver creates.
+It marks each vap with
+.Dv IEEE80211_FEXT_SCAN_OFFLOAD
+and
+.Dv IEEE80211_ROAMING_DEVICE ,
+so that
+.Xr ieee80211 9
+neither scans in software nor roams on its own.
+Its state hangs off the
+.Va ic_fmac
+member of
+.Vt struct ieee80211com .
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_detach
+undoes the attach and must be called before
+.Xr ieee80211_ifdetach 9 .
+.Ss Operations
+The
+.Vt ieee80211_fullmac_ops
+structure holds the calls the framework makes into the driver.
+Each returns 0 on success or an error number.
+The framework calls them from process or
+.Xr taskqueue 9
+context, never from an interrupt, and they may sleep.
+A driver leaves an optional operation
+.Dv NULL ;
+the operations it fills in decide what the device offers, and there are
+no separate capability flags.
+.Bl -tag -width "fmop_extauth_status"
+.It Va fmop_name
+A short name for the driver, used in messages.
+Required.
+.It Va fmop_scan_start
+Start a firmware scan, active or passive, optionally for one SSID.
+The driver reports each network found with
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_scan_result
+and the end of the scan with
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_scan_done .
+Required.
+.It Va fmop_scan_cancel
+Stop a scan that
+.Xr ieee80211 9
+ended while the firmware was still running it.
+.It Va fmop_assoc
+Join the network described by a
+.Vt struct ieee80211_fmac_assoc :
+the BSSID, SSID and channel
+.Xr ieee80211 9
+chose, and the WPA or RSN element
+.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
+supplied.
+Required.
+.It Va fmop_disassoc
+Leave the current network with the given 802.11 reason code.
+Required.
+.It Va fmop_set_key , Va fmop_del_key
+Install or remove a key.
+The framework reaches these through the vap's
+.Va iv_key_set
+and
+.Va iv_key_delete
+methods.
+.Va fmop_set_key
+is required.
+.It Va fmop_set_country
+Set the firmware's country to the two-letter code the user configured.
+.It Va fmop_set_pmk
+Give the firmware's own supplicant a 32-byte PMK.
+When present, the framework adds a write-only
+.Va net.wlan.N.fullmac_pmk
+sysctl.
+.It Va fmop_set_powersave
+Turn power save on or off.
+When present, the framework sets
+.Dv IEEE80211_C_PMGT .
+.It Va fmop_get_signal
+Report the current signal and noise of the associated access point in
+dBm.
+The framework polls it every two seconds while a station is associated.
+.It Va fmop_start_ap , Va fmop_stop_ap
+Start or stop an access point described by a
+.Vt struct ieee80211_fmac_ap .
+When both are present, the framework sets
+.Dv IEEE80211_C_HOSTAP .
+.It Va fmop_sta_deauth
+Send a station away from the access point.
+.It Va fmop_sta_idle
+Report how long the firmware has not heard from a station, so that
+.Xr ieee80211 9
+can age stations as usual.
+.It Va fmop_mgmt_tx , Va fmop_extauth_status
+External SAE for a station.
+.Va fmop_mgmt_tx
+sends an Authentication frame built by
+.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 ,
+and
+.Va fmop_extauth_status
+passes on the result of the exchange.
+Both must be present or both absent.
+.It Va fmop_set_pmksa
+Load the list of cached PMKSAs into the firmware.
+.El
+.Ss Up-calls
+The driver calls these when the firmware reports an event.
+.Bl -tag -width "ieee80211_fmac_assoc_reject"
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_scan_result
+One network found by a scan, described by a
+.Vt struct ieee80211_fmac_bss
+that holds the information elements as the firmware reported them.
+The framework adds the entry to the
+.Xr ieee80211_scan 9
+cache.
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_scan_done
+The firmware finished the scan.
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_link_up
+The firmware joined the network; the framework moves the vap to
+.Dv IEEE80211_S_RUN .
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_link_down
+The link was lost, with an 802.11 reason code.
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_roamed
+The firmware moved to another access point of the same network.
+The framework moves the station and sends
+.Dv RTM_IEEE80211_REASSOC .
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_rx
+An Ethernet frame from the firmware, data or EAPOL.
+The framework passes it to the vap and consumes the mbuf.
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_sta_join , Fn ieee80211_fmac_sta_leave
+A station joined or left the access point.
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_extauth_req
+The firmware wants the host to run SAE with an access point.
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_mgmt_rx
+An Authentication frame received for the host's SAE exchange.
+.It Fn ieee80211_fmac_assoc_reject
+The firmware gave up on a join, with an 802.11 status code.
+.El
+.Pp
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_link_up ,
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_link_down
+and
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_roamed
+may call driver operations and must be called from a context that can
+sleep.
+The other up-calls copy what they need and return at once, and are safe
+from the driver's event path.
+.Ss Userland interface
+For external SAE and PMKSA caching the framework adds three routing
+socket messages,
+.Dv RTM_IEEE80211_EXTAUTH ,
+.Dv RTM_IEEE80211_MGMT_RX
+and
+.Dv RTM_IEEE80211_ASSOC_REJECT ,
+and four
+.Dv SIOCS80211
+requests,
+.Dv IEEE80211_IOC_MGMT_TX ,
+.Dv IEEE80211_IOC_EXTAUTH_STATUS ,
+.Dv IEEE80211_IOC_EXTAUTH_CAPS
+and
+.Dv IEEE80211_IOC_PMKSA .
+They are defined in
+.In net80211/ieee80211_freebsd.h
+and
+.In net80211/ieee80211_ioctl.h .
+.Sh RETURN VALUES
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_attach
+returns 0 on success.
+It returns
+.Er EINVAL
+if a required operation or
+.Va ic_vap_create
+is missing, or if only one of
+.Va fmop_mgmt_tx
+and
+.Va fmop_extauth_status
+is set, and
+.Er EBUSY
+if the device is already attached.
+.Pp
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_link_up ,
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_link_down
+and
+.Fn ieee80211_fmac_roamed
+return 0 on success, and
+.Er ENOENT
+when no station vap is in a state to take the event.
+.Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr bwfm 4 ,
+.Xr wlan 4 ,
+.Xr ieee80211 9 ,
+.Xr ieee80211_crypto 9 ,
+.Xr ieee80211_proto 9 ,
+.Xr ieee80211_scan 9 ,
+.Xr ieee80211_vap 9
+.Sh HISTORY
+The
+.Nm
+framework first appeared in
+.Fx 16.0 .
+.Sh AUTHORS
+.An Kyle Crenshaw Aq Mt b1nc0d3x@gmail.com
